    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="8">
        <head>Af Rb 8</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="16" ed="#liebermann"/>IX. Be nunnan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Rubrics-Af_8.lnote.oe.10"/> hæmede.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-ot-frag"><pb n="16" ed="#liebermann"/>… nnan hæmede.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-g-prol"><pb n="16" ed="#liebermann"/>IX. Be nunnan hæmede.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="17" ed="#liebermann"/>IX. Be nunnan hæmede.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="17" ed="#liebermann"/>De nunne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Rubrics-Af_8.lnote.oe.7"/> concubitu.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="188" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>IX Be nunnan hæmede</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="188" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Be ða<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þe nunnan of mynstre ut alædeð</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="17" ed="#liebermann"/>Von geschlechtlicher Verbindung mit einer Nonne.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Rubrics-Af_8.lnote.de.1"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Of sexual intercourse with a nun.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="189" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Concerning having intercourse with a nun</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="189" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Concerning one who leads a nun out of a minster</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Af_8.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">17</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">c. n. <hi rend="italic">T;</hi> De ducente sanctimonialem ab ecclesia <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">c. n. T; De ducente sanctimonialem ab ecclesia Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Af_8.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">16</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðam ðe nu. of minster út alædaþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi> [<hi rend="italic">aus B</hi>]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðam ðe nu. of minster út alædaþ Ld [from B]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Rubrics-Af_8.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Schmid übersetzt aus Hs. B: ‘Von dem der eine Nonne aus dem Kloster entführt’; B aber bildet, von der Rubrikenliste abweichend, sich selbst eine Überschrift aus Af-Texte, hier und öfter: was ich weiterhin nicht bemerke</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Schmid translates from MS B: ‘Of him who abducts a nun from the convent’; but B, departing from the list of rubrics, forms a heading of its own from the text of Af, here and often: which I do not note hereafter</seg></note>
      </div>
